id: pm-vcs-5h6j
title: "Phase 5: the forge and the patch series"
description: "Forgejo is right that project metadata belongs inside the repository, and the kernel's lore workflow is right that a change under review is a first-class object with a lifecycle. This phase makes both native: a patch series is an object kind, review state is a record, and a served repository exposes them so agents can propose, review and land changes without a second system holding the state."
type: Epic
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:25.155Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-14T21:33:19.288Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "A patch series can be produced from a commit range, transferred, applied and re-derived byte-identically; review state is a record that merges per field so two reviewers never conflict; a served repository exposes refs, objects and series over the transport from Phase 3; End-to-end served-forge tests deny every cross-tenant object and ref read write copy list and update operation without leaking object existence; Publication is rejected when a required stable-FileId lock lease is missing expired owned by another principal or outside its branch scope"
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-tr2a,parent,"2026-07-31T06:28:27.601Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
  pm-vcs-ag8y,blocked_by,"2026-08-01T19:52:24.568Z",codex,review-finding,asserted
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T15:48:57.654Z",claude,"Two of five children are complete and closed: the patch series as a native object kind, and review state as a per-field-merging record. The remaining three stay open with written specs rather than half-built: the served repository over the Phase 3 transport, cross-tenant denial without existence leakage, and publication refusing without a valid stable-FileId lock lease. The epic stays open until they land."
  "2026-08-28T20:11:17.158Z",pi-agent,"PR #48 evidence: commit 4ddd53c implements the patch-series and review-record vertical slice. Local npm test passed 675 of 675 tests. npm run release:check passed with c8 at 100 percent statements branches functions and lines. The three deferred children remain open by design and are linked in the PR description."
  "2026-09-12T23:35:59.128Z",pi-agent,"Audit 2026-09-13: EXISTS — patch series production from a commit range, transfer, apply, and re-derivation are implemented and tested (engine/series.ts, test/series.test.ts: 'a series produced from a commit range references the correct commits in order', 're-deriving a series from the same range produces a byte-identical object id', 'a transferred series re-derived from the same commits in a fresh store is byte-identical', 'applying a series to a fresh branch produces commits with the same trees'). Review state as a record that merges per field is implemented (engine/review.ts, test/review.test.ts: 'two reviewers writing different fields of one review record merge cleanly'). REMAINS — a served repository exposing refs, objects and series over the transport is not implemented (pm-vcs-ttc0 spec only). Cross-tenant denial without existence leakage is not implemented (pm-vcs-4ff1 spec only, no tenant code). Publication rejection without a valid stable-FileId lock lease is not implemented (pm-vcs-hre2 spec only, no lease code). Three of five acceptance criteria are not met."
  "2026-10-14T19:47:13.386Z",codex-agent,"Phase 5 pre-implementation audit at origin/main 3fdba73:\n| Criterion | Implementing files | Existing test names | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Produce, transfer, apply, re-derive byte-identically | engine/series.ts, engine/model.ts, engine/bundle.ts | test/series.test.ts: a transferred series re-derived from the same commits in a fresh store is byte-identical; applying a series to a fresh branch produces commits with the same trees; test/served-sync.test.ts: a series object transfers through the served repository's verified-arrival path | Partial: engine round trip exists; no served series catalog or client workflow |\n| Review records merge per field | engine/review.ts, engine/records.ts | test/review.test.ts: two reviewers writing different fields of one review record merge cleanly; a genuinely conflicting scalar field is reported as a conflict while other fields still merge | Partial: local merge exists; served concurrent field updates and recorded deterministic same-field resolution missing |\n| Served refs, objects and series over Phase 3 transport | engine/serve.ts, engine/http-transport.ts, engine/transport.ts | test/served-sync.test.ts: fetch and push over HTTP answer exactly as they do against a file remote; a series object transfers through the served repository's verified-arrival path | Partial: refs/objects served; series can travel as unnamed objects but no list/fetch/publish/update series or reviews API |\n| All cross-tenant reads/writes/copies/lists/updates deny without existence oracle | engine/serve.ts, engine/served-repositories.ts | test/serve.test.ts: every refusal a caller may not learn from answers with the same bytes; unauthenticated and out-of-scope requests never refresh the real catalogue; filesystem aliases cannot make one tenant serve another tenant's repository | Partial: current endpoints pre-authorize; real server-process operation matrix for series/reviews and timing-class regression missing |\n| Missing/expired/foreign/out-of-scope FileId leases reject publication | engine/publication-leases.ts, engine/transport.ts, engine/serve.ts | test/publication-leases.test.ts: filesystem publication refuses missing, expired, scope and stale fencing proofs without moving refs; authenticated HTTP uses receiver principals, explicit break grants and preserves typed refusal fields | Partial: ref enforcement implemented; extend to series publication and prove all four typed refusals through a real served process |\nPlan: native series/review roots, authenticated bounded forge endpoints and client commands; reuse native record merge and receiver leases. No Phase 6 implementation and no dependency pin changes."
  "2026-10-14T20:09:05.237Z",codex-agent,"Phase 5 delivered evidence matrix. All eight focused scenarios pass, including real server-process and installed CLI acceptance. Full per-file coverage and release gates are being run separately.\n| Criterion | Files | Real proving test names in test/served-forge.test.ts | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Commit range -> transfer -> apply -> byte-identical rederive | engine/series.ts, engine/bundle.ts, engine/forge.ts, forge-commands.ts | installed pm vcs commands propose fetch apply rederive review and land through a real served process; series bundles include fragment closure and rederive identical binary proposal bytes in a fresh served store | Met |\n| Native review fields merge concurrently and disagreements are recorded | engine/review.ts, engine/records.ts, engine/forge.ts | served forge concurrent reviewers preserve disjoint fields and record deterministic same-field outcomes; native forge CAS updates reset review state and reject foreign or stale review bases | Met |\n| Serve refs, objects, named series and reviews through Phase 3 | engine/serve.ts, engine/http-protocol.ts, engine/http-transport.ts, engine/transport.ts, engine/forge.ts, forge-commands.ts | installed pm vcs commands propose fetch apply rederive review and land through a real served process; extension forge command defaults explicit remotes and refusal paths use real native repositories; existing test/served-sync.test.ts fetch and push over HTTP answer exactly as they do against a file remote | Met |\n| Tenant-safe read/write/copy/list/update for every resource, absent equivalence and timing class | engine/serve.ts, engine/http-protocol.ts, engine/served-repositories.ts | real served process denies every cross-tenant object ref series and review operation without an existence oracle; forge envelopes reject malformed operations names revisions scopes and review patches before catalog access | Met |\n| Required stable-FileId lease ownership/expiry/branch scope at publication | engine/publication-leases.ts, engine/transport.ts, engine/forge.ts | real served forge and ref publication reject missing expired foreign and out-of-branch leases with typed reasons | Met |\nLinked pm test runs: pm-vcs-ttqa 4/4, pm-vcs-6e5m 1/1, pm-vcs-mv7e 3/3; all exit 0 with zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo. Test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so receipts are recorded in comments without changing that policy.\nBehavioral authorization rollback fails with a missing forbidden rejection. Targeted per-field mediation rollback fails with lost approval/reviewer fields. Code restored after both proofs. Same-field canonical-min outcomes must be inspected before landing; the forge intentionally leaves approval policy to agents. Earlier native proposal and review history survives GC after lease release."
  "2026-10-14T20:35:52.882Z",codex-agent,"Final focused verification: all 10 served-forge scenarios pass with zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. After rebuilding the same source snapshot, engine/forge.ts and forge-commands.ts meet per-file 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Applied-HEAD rederivation is now asserted explicitly. The earlier full run's sole behavioral test failure was the fixed 63-to-65 inventory assertion; mixed source snapshots made its new-module coverage report invalid. Committed-source npm and Bun release checks are next."
  "2026-10-14T21:33:10.485Z",codex-agent,"Implementation commit 97375e18844a188bb98c5110cec65194cb25b03b verified. npm run release:check with a fresh HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1: exit 0, 1523/1523 tests. bun run release:check: exit 0, 1523/1523 tests. Both: zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo; per-file 100% statements/branches/functions/lines over all 65 production files; zero lint warnings, 0% duplicates, 354 documented declarations; native TOON, stat-cache strace, committed self-host equality, production audit, Git identities, pack dry run, full changelog check, release date and publish attestation all pass. Ten served-forge scenarios pass, with real server-process tenant/lease evidence and applied-HEAD byte-identical rederivation. Authorization and field-merge behavioral rollbacks failed as expected, then current code was restored and rebuilt. No dependency pins changed and no Phase 6 implementation was added."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-01T19:32:32.287Z",codex,Epic Lore change requests are distinct from the kernel-lore patch-series workflow. The served forge must authorize every object and ref operation inside tenant-isolated repository partitions and enforce stable-file-ID lock leases at publication.
